I fixed #1107 and committed it (02e05e19). yoyo diff --cahced now stops with exit 2 instead of quietly showing a different diff. The full test suite, clippy with -D warnings, and the fmt check all pass.

The bug: both yoyo diff and /diff use the same argument parser, and it silently dropped any flag it didn't recognise. In a temp repo with one staged and one unstaged change, I confirmed --cahced printed both changes and exited 0. --cached showed only the staged one.

What changed
• Parser (src/commands_git.rs): it now records the first flag it doesn't recognise. I added a field rather than returning an error so none of the parser's four callers had to change.
• `yoyo diff`: prints this on stderr and exits 2 without running git:
  usage: yoyo diff [--staged|--cached] [--name-only] [--stat] [--functions] [<file>|<rev>|<rev>..<rev>]
  unknown flag: --cahced
  The usage line doesn't mention --explain. The parser accepts it, but the shell has no AI session to explain anything with.
• `/diff`: the same refusal in /diff terms (it does list [--explain]) and no git command. This also covers /diff --explain --bogus, which goes through a different code path.
• `--`: now accepted as the path separator. A word starting with - after it isn't refused; it's still ignored, exactly as before.

Tests
• A new sibling file, src/commands_git_diff_flag_tests.rs, checks the refusals on both doors. It also checks that every accepted input parses exactly as before, field by field: each accepted flag, HEAD~1..HEAD, zzz (which still goes to git as a revision), and a path after --.
• A test in tests/integration.rs runs the built binary in a temp repo. --cahced gives exit 2 with nothing on stdout, and --cached still shows only the staged change.
• To check the new tests can actually fail, I disabled the parser change. The two refusal tests failed and the rest stayed green. I restored the code in the same command, and no disabled-code marker remains.

Other files
• `tests/module_size.rs`: commands_git.rs went from 3822 to 3858 lines, one line under the size limit (registered 3809 + 50). I raised its registered size to 3858 and the comment explains why: 13 lines were already over the old figure before this task, and 36 are this fix.
• Docs: I added a line to CHANGELOG.md and a sentence to the exit-code paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md.
• #1107 references: git grep '#1107\b' finds only three code comments describing this fix. Nothing user-facing points at the ticket, so closing it leaves no dead pointers.
